meta {
  name: Print All Order Reports
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/order/{{orderId}}/print-all
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "templateId": "{{pdfReportTemplateId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Render ALL of an order's reports into one consolidated PDF (`lab_all_report`),
  streamed back as `application/pdf`. Aggregates every active report for the order
  into a single `{{#each reports}}` section (one row per test, with a joined result
  summary), plus the de-duplicated approving signatories in the footer
  (`<signing_authority_tag>`).

  ## Body
  - `templateId` (optional) — the `lab_all_report` template to render with. Omit to
    fall back to the tenant's single active `lab_all_report` template.

  ## Related
  - `POST /lab-reports/:id/print` renders a SINGLE report. Its body now also
    accepts an optional `type` (`lab_report` | `lab_panel`, default `lab_report`),
    used only to resolve the default template when no `templateId` is given — the
    same report record renders either way.

  ## Errors
  - 404 `LAB_REPORT_NOT_FOUND` — the order has no reports.
  - 404 `NO_ACTIVE_PRINT_TEMPLATE` / 409 `AMBIGUOUS_PRINT_TEMPLATE` — template
    resolution failed and no `templateId` was supplied.

  In Bruno, use "Save Response → Save to file" to inspect the PDF.
}
